<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kirghiz SSR</h1><p class="st-meta">1936 CE – 1991 CE · capital Frunze</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Soviet republic of the Kyrgyz in the Tian Shan, the direct forerunner of today's Kyrgyzstan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under the Soviet constitution of December 1936 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kazakh-assr">Kirghiz ASSR</a> was made a union republic, the Kirghiz SSR, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishkek">Frunze</a>, the former Pishpek and today's Bishkek.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was a land of mountain pastures, livestock farming, mining and some industry, with a large Russian population in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishkek">Frunze</a> and the north and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbeks</a> in the south around Osh. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrgyz-people">Kyrgyz</a> culture was promoted in Soviet form, including the epic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epic-of-manas">Manas</a> and the novels of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chingiz-aitmatov">Chingiz Aitmatov</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turdakun-usubaliyev">Turdakun Usubaliyev</a> led the party from 1961 to 1985. Ethnic clashes between Kyrgyz and Uzbeks in Osh in 1990 killed hundreds.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The physicist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askar-akayev">Askar Akayev</a> became president in 1990. After the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> coup, the republic declared independence on 31 August 1991 as the Republic of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kyrgyzstan">Kyrgyzstan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kirghiz-ssr.jpg" alt="Kirghiz SSR" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kirghiz_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1952%E2%80%931991);_Flag_of_Kyrgyzstan_(1991%E2%80%931992).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1936 CE – 1991 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Frunze</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Turdakun Usubaliyev, Askar Akayev</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (state atheism)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kyrgyz, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kyrgyzstan">Kyrgyzstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kirghiz Soviet Socialist Republic, Kyrgyz SSR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=kirghiz-ssr" aria-label="Kirghiz SSR on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6483 655 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kirghiz SSR lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6803 911L6802 911M6803 911L5820 533M6803 911L6802 911"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6802 911h0M5820 533h0M6802 911h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6803 911h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6803 911h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=kirghiz-ssr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
